cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kanchi TEI: a demonstration edition pipeline for South Indian temple legends"
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Note that the sample text carried by this repository is synthetic and must
  not be cited as an edition of any historical work.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ani
    family-names: Chandrashekhar
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/kanchi-tei"
abstract: >-
  A working demonstration of a digital scholarly edition pipeline: TEI P5
  sources with a parallel-segmentation critical apparatus, a schema generated
  from a TEI ODD, an eXist-db application publishing the corpus over RESTXQ,
  XSLT transformations to HTML and CIDOC-CRM RDF, and a Python service for
  Devanagari and Tamil script conversion.
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - TEI
  - XML
  - eXist-db
  - XQuery
  - XSLT
  - Linked Open Data
  - CIDOC-CRM
  - Sanskrit
  - Tamil
  - critical edition
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-31"
